WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.600
Good morning, Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.160
Who drew it? Daddy or Henry?

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:04.660
Daddy.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:07.460
It's question Tuesday, the day that I answer real questions from real nerdfighters,

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:08.600
but first a story.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.520
So Hank, almost every morning I wake up with a song in my head,

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.440
also you might remember that I once described tumblr

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.960
as being comprised primarily of

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.780
homoerotic "Who-lock" watercolors.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:19.100
Okay, so then my dutch friends Lotte and Lidewij wrote a song about it for me,

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.400
and this morning I woke up and I was walking around and I was singing:

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.480
♫ Homoerotic water colors are just one thing ♫

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.240
♫ I love they do not define me you should know. ♫

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:32.960
And then I looked over at the living room at Henry's babysitter was there and she was like "whaaaaat?"

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:33.460
But it's true though.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:37.120
By the way, Hank, I just looked down and I was like "Fried chicken? Here in the morning!?"

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.380
"What have I done to deserve this?"

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:39.659
But it turns out it's play chicken.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.180
It's so weird having a toddler.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:41.840
Right, it's question Tuesday.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:45.820
But I have to go into the office which means the quality of this video is about to...

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:47.840
improve significantly.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:49.180
Favorite part of the evening of awesome?

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.320
The part where all of it.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.360
What would you most like to tell Esther about?

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:53.980
I really wish she could have read the Fault in Our Stars,

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:55.820
I think all the time about whether she would have liked it.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:56.900
Finish this sentence:

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.880
It would be a privilege to have my heart broken by...

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:01.469
Pizza. The answer is always pizza.

00:01:01.469 --> 00:01:04.620
Hey, how do I know if someone wants to be just friends or more than friends?

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:05.740
Yeah, you should use your words.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:08.020
But wait, what do you mean "just friends" and "more than friends?"

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:10.360
Like, when did we hardwire into our language

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:12.780
the idea that the step past friendship

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:14.400
is mutual face licking?

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:18.760
Like the Yeti and I are "more than friends" not primarily because of the face licking aspect of things

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:21.920
but because there are important things that we share responsibility for,

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:25.300
like a car and a mortgage and a human child.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:28.600
Like this is Shannon, and we lived together for more than five years in our twenties,

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:32.680
and I really take offense at the notion that we're "just friends" simply because we never made out.

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:36.140
I mean Shannon and I have been together for the worst and best days of each other's lives.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:38.760
We're not "just friends," we're not "just" anything.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:40.460
So yeah, you shouldn't say do you want to be more than friends,

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:41.640
You should say what you mean.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:42.244
You should say

00:01:42.244 --> 00:01:44.380
"Do you want to be monogamous face licking partners?"

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:47.100
And yes, I realize that not all romantic relationships involve making out,

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.880
but you should say what you mean.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:51.580
Why is your tumblr called fishing boat proceeds?

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:52.580
Ever since 2007,

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:54.240
I've been trying to get some fishing boat proceeds

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:57.020
because then you get to check off a special box on your tax return,

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:00.089
But it hasn't happened, so I figured maybe through tumblr, but not yet.

00:02:00.089 --> 00:02:02.400
Are you ever afraid of running out of ideas for books

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.980
or getting writer's block so crippling that you never write again?

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.860
Yes, and thank you for mentioning it.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.360
Wherefore art thou Romeo?

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.480
Because as I explained in a recent episode of Crash Course,

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:14.080
if he were named Paris he wouldn't be nearly so hot.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:16.180
Does Holden Caufield ever change?

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:19.260
I'm starting to think you just aren't subscribed to Crash Course, which, you really should be.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:20.100
TFiOS movie?

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:20.780
I love the script.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:22.050
I don't think I'm allowed to say anything else,

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:23.340
I'm not even sure I'm allowed to say that.

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:24.700
So just pretend I didn't say anything.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:27.100
Do you have any tips for a scared parent-to-be?

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:30.660
Yeah, so at first everyone feels totally unqualified to be a parent

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:36.000
But then you realize "all I have to do is trick this baby into thinking I'm qualified to be a parent."

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:36.900
This is a baby!

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.740
In some cases, they were literally born yesterday.

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:41.340
They're super easy to trick!

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:42.880
Nerdfighters, whether you were at Carnegie Hall,

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:44.429
or watched an evening of awesome at home,

00:02:44.429 --> 00:02:45.800
thank you so much.

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.480
It was the highlight of my professional career.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:51.140
Hank, thanks for making it fun and surprisingly relaxing,

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:53.960
You are made of awesome, I will see you on Friday.

